  "body": "## Cause\n\nThe post-merge run 44780029308 (main `768fe23f0`) failed in `contract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times` (`crates/app/tests/example_catalog/contract.rs:59`). The step log (artifact `gate-logs-post-merge-44780029308-1`, `494-app_suites_example_catalog.log`) shows:\n\n```\nmissing time for 2d/contour-tabs:\n...\ncatalog 2d/contour-tabs regenerates\nthread '<unnamed>' (1052938) panicked at crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs:68:5:\n2d/first-part: missing model/\n elapsed=0.000s budget=60.000s\n```\n\n- The scratch-root override works. The inner cases fail in 0.000 s on the empty root.\n- The inner run starts the two cases in parallel.\n- `within` wrote its timing line with `writeln!` to stderr. Stderr has no buffer, so the line went out in pieces.\n- The panic message of the other case thread fell between the pieces. The assert did not find `catalog 2d/contour-tabs regenerates elapsed=`.\n\nThis is a race. It occurs more on the loaded Linux runner. The 59 s is the time of the full binary, not of this test.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs`: the new `timing_line` makes the whole line with its newline. `within` writes it with one `write_all` on the locked stderr.\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/contract.rs`: the inner run uses `--test-threads=1`. The two cases run in order. The asserts do not change.\n- `docs/decisions/3043-catalog-timing-line.md`: the decision, and what was dropped (a retry, a looser assert).\n\n## Pins\n\n- `contract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times` (the red test).\n- `support::timing_line_is_one_whole_line` (new).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNot built locally: the local build slot was in use. The PR test runner and the coordinator's gate run it.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3043\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
